.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
*.tfstate.lock.info
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfvars.local
.envrc.local

# Per-env vars hold publishable Supabase keys + domain config —
# keep them out of git. The tfvars.example files are committed as
# templates.
envs/*/terraform.tfvars

# FAIL-SAFE: this repo is PUBLIC. Production sops ciphertext must NEVER be
# committed here — it lives in the private estate repo Absence0760/infra-secrets
# (cloned at ../infra-secrets), one subdir per project. Even encrypted, a sops
# file in public history leaks KMS-ARN metadata + the exact secret key names, and
# is the mistake the docs explicitly warn against. These patterns guarantee an
# operator running an old/local flow can't accidentally `git add` ciphertext.
secrets.enc.yaml
envs/*/secrets.enc.yaml
**/secrets.enc.yaml
# Decrypted scratch (sops decrypts to memory; guard the common accidental names).
*.dec
*.dec.*
*.decrypted
*.decrypted.*
*.plain
*.plain.*
